# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MenuQR — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development and fill
# in real values. Never commit `.env.local` or any file containing
# real secrets to version control.
#
# This is a SEPARATE application from the repo's wedding-invitations
# app — it needs its own Supabase project (its database schema is
# entirely different) and its own env vars. Do not point it at the
# same Supabase project used by the root app.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Supabase project URL and anon key are safe to expose to the browser.
# Multi-tenant isolation (a restaurant can never see another restaurant's
# data) is enforced by Postgres Row Level Security policies — see
# supabase/migrations/ for the full policy set. Without these two vars the
# app still runs; every page and form falls back to a friendly
# "not configured" state instead of crashing, but nothing is persisted.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Public site URL — used to build QR code target URLs, canonical links,
# the sitemap, and Open Graph metadata. No trailing slash.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
